        <briefdescription>
<para>Load (or replace) the ONNX cross-encoder model. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Load Model.</para>
<para>The loader canonicalises <computeroutput>model_path</computeroutput>, rejects symlinks, requires a regular <computeroutput>.onnx</computeroutput> file, validates bounded file size and permissions, and computes a SHA-256 digest before accepting the model. When a <computeroutput>&lt;model_path&gt;.sha256</computeroutput> sidecar exists, the digest must match; when the sidecar is absent, the loader emits a warning and proceeds.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>model_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Path to the ONNX model file. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> when the model passed validation and was loaded; <computeroutput>false</computeroutput> on invalid paths, checksum mismatches, or other integrity/safety failures.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">model_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Path to the model. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True when the operation succeeds.</para>
</simplesect>
Calls: empty(), THEMIS_WARN(), input_path(), std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(), THEMIS_ERROR(), std::filesystem::is_symlink(), extension(), verifyModelFile(). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
